**Summary of the recommendation:** Redis Streams, rejected Kafka. The decisive factors were team constraints (6 people, no Kafka experience, 2-week window) and existing Redis infrastructure — not raw throughput. The exactly-once requirement is addressed via a PostgreSQL dedup table, which is the correct approach regardless of transport choice. Kafka would be premature infrastructure at this scale (500 req/s peak, 10x growth still fits Redis comfortably).
